     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's about twice the usual maximum:\n\n- **Immediate-release:** the maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Many references use 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day.\n- **Extended-release:** the maximum is 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n\nAt this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is high, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- Another dose. If so, tell me the intended dose and frequency.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily really is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
